 ## Overview
-The Neural Duplex Radiance Field is a real-time view synthesis method that replaces dense volumetric ray marching with a two-surface proxy representation. It solves the computational bottleneck of evaluating deep MLPs for every sample point by learning to map the two endpoints of a ray segment (defined by intersections with inner and outer meshes) and the view direction to the final pixel color. It sets itself apart from its parent [NeRF Network Query with Hashed Embeddings](3107-nerf-network-query-with-hashed-embeddings.md) by abandoning per-point MLP queries in favor of vertex-attached features interpolated via hardware rasterization, and from siblings like [HybridNeRF Model Architecture](4842-hybridnerf-model-architecture.md) by relying on explicit mesh proxies rather than hybrid voxel/grid structures for the primary geometry.
+The Neural Duplex Radiance Field is a real-time view synthesis method that replaces dense volumetric ray marching with a two-surface proxy representation [S1]. It solves the computational bottleneck of evaluating deep MLPs for every sample point by learning to map the two endpoints of a ray segment (defined by intersections with inner and outer meshes) and the view direction to the final pixel color [S1]. It sets itself apart from its parent [NeRF Network Query with Hashed Embeddings](3107-nerf-network-query-with-hashed-embeddings.md) by abandoning per-point MLP queries in favor of vertex-attached features interpolated via hardware rasterization, and from siblings like [HybridNeRF Model Architecture](4842-hybridnerf-model-architecture.md) by relying on explicit mesh proxies rather than hybrid voxel/grid structures for the primary geometry [S1].
 
 ## How it works
